Woolly contains no code from other memory projects. Some of its designs were
adapted from these Apache-2.0 projects, with thanks:

- claude-mem (https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem): capturing coding
  sessions through lifecycle hooks, and a small brief at session start with
  details fetched on demand.
- Mem0 (https://github.com/mem0ai/mem0): the add, update, delete and no-op
  decision for each new fact, and the shape of its memory API.
- Graphiti by Zep (https://github.com/getzep/graphiti): facts that record when
  they became true and when they stopped being true.
- Letta (https://github.com/letta-ai/letta): editing memory in the background
  while the agent is idle, which Woolly calls dreaming.
